Replaced the base copy constructor, which copies the entire fixed-size value buffer, with the default constructor plus a copy of only the used `size` bytes. This avoids copying up to 255 bytes for every field when most fields are much smaller.

```include
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase()
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
    num = field.num;
    size = field.size;
    std::memcpy(value, field.value, size);
}
```